N2  - The proceedings contain 290 papers. The topics discussed include: patisiran in patients with hATTR amyloidosis post-orthotopic liver transplant: 12-month results; automation of quantifying axonal loss through MRI and deep learning in patients with peripheral neuropathies; cross-sectional area reference values for peripheral nerve ultrasound in adults: a systematic review and metanalysis - part I: upper extremity nerve; cross-sectional area reference values for peripheral nerve ultrasound in adults: a systematic review and meta-analysis - part III: cervical nerve root; HELIOS-A: 9-month results from the phase 3 study of vutrisiran in patients with hereditary transthyretin-mediated amyloidosis with polyneuropathy; relation of exercise and pain in patients with idiopathic distal axonal polyneuropathies; valency dictates anti-Nfasc155 IgG4 pathogenicity; improvement of intractable common peroneal neuroma pain with a more proximal nerve block: a case report; defective vestibular function may contribute to severe sensory ataxia in PMP22-related congenital peripheral hypomyelination; and personalized biopsychosocial treatment for small fiber neuropathy, a study protocol.
