A1  - Poulsen P.
A1  - Andersen H.
Y1  - 2017//
N2  - Objective: To evaluate if diffusion-tensor-imaging MR-Neurography (DTIMRN) can detect lesions of peripheral nerves in patients with type 1 diabetes. Background(s): Diabetic peripheral neuropathy (DPN) often remains undiagnosed until advanced stages. DPN causes irreversible damage to the peripheral nerves. Early diagnosis and sensitive diagnostic techniques are needed. Method(s): Forty-nine type 1 diabetic patients (11 with severe polyneuropathy (sDPN), 13 with mild/moderate polyneuropathy (mDPN) and 25 without polyneuropathy (nDPN)) and 30 healthy controls (HC) were included. Clinical examinations, nerve-conduction-studies and vibratory-perception-thresholds described the presence and severity of DPN. DTI-MRN (voxel size: 1.4x1.4x3mm3; b-values: 0, 800 s/mm2) covered proximal (sciatic nerve) and distal regions of the lower extremity (tibial nerve). FA and ADC were calculated and compared to T2 relaxometry and proton-spin-density obtained from a multi-echo TSE sequence. Result(s): DTI-MRN could accurately discriminate between DPN, nDPN and HC. The proximal FA was lowest in sDPN (sDPN 0.38+/-0.04; mDPN 0.41+/-0.07; nDPN 0.47+/-0.02; HC 0.48+/-0.06; p<0.01). In addition, distal FA was lowest in sDPN (sDPN 0.31+/-0.08; mDPN 0.34+/-0.06; nDPN 0.41+/-0.07; HC 0.42+/-0.07; p<0.01). Likewise, proximal ADC was highest in sDPN with lower values in patients with mPDN and nDPN as well as in HC. The severity of neuropathy was correlated to DTI-MRN with a strong association of proximal (FA: R2 = 0.49, p<0.01; ADC: R2 = 0.15, p = 0.01) and distal nerve lesions (FA: R2 = 0.32, p< 0.01; ADC: R2 = 0.19; p-value < 0.01). Conclusion(s): DTI-MRN enables detection of DPN by decreasing nerve FA and increasing ADC closely related to the severity of DPN. These findings may reflect proximal and distal nerve fibre pathology. We shall further develop this novel approach for use in clinical studies and clinical practice. Previous data from our group was presented at the ADA 2016 Scientific Sessions.
