T1  - Diffusion tensor imaging as a functional measure in determination of peripheral nerve lesions in CIDP treated with subcutaneous immunoglobulin
T3  - 68th American Academy of Neurology Annual Meeting, AAN 2016. Vancouver, BC Canada.
A1  - Jakobsen J.
A1  - Vaeggemose M.
A1  - Andersen H.
A1  - Markvardsen L.
Y1  - 2016//
N2  - Objective: To evaluate if the MRI technique diffusion tensor imaging can detect nerve lesions in Chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy (CIDP) patients treated with subcutaneous immunoglobulin (SCIG) Background: CIDP is diagnosed based on neurophysiological and clinical examination. Studies have shown that MRI of peripheral nerves can detect lesion in several types of polyneuropathy. Previously, it has been shown that Fractional Anisotropy (FA) is decreased in the tibial nerve from a mixed group of CIDP patients. Method(s): MRI of the sciatic and tibial nerves was performed at thigh and shin using the knee coil on a 3T Siemens Magnetom Skyra MR-scanner. At both thigh and shin one cross section was selected for imaging. Twenty slices were obtained (slice thickness/distance 4:2 mm) performing T2- and DTI-weighted MRI sequences with fat saturation. Data from DTI-weighted images served for pixel-by-pixel calculation of FA and Apparent Diffusion Coefficient (ADC). Circular region-of-interest (ROI) was segmented around the tibial and sciatic nerves at each image slice with reference to the T2-weighted images. Average FA- and ADC-values were calculated from the nerve ROI. Result(s): All CIDP patients (n=14) were treated with SCIG (Gammanorm). Healthy controls (n=14) were gender and age matched. FA-values of the tibial and the sciatic nerve were decreased in CIDP versus controls (0.34+/-0.07 vs 0.42+/-0.07 (P<0.0001) and 0.42+/-0.07 vs 0.48+/-0.03 (P<0.0001)). Correspondingly, ADC-values in tibial and sciatic nerve were increased in CIDP versus control (1833+/-277 vs 1648+/-175 (P<0.0001) and (1648+/-175 vs 1568+/-83 (P<0.05)). The sciatic/tibial ratio of the FA-map showed no difference comparing CIDP and controls (1.25+/-0.24 vs 1.16+/-0.15 (P=0.09)) but significant changes were found for the ADC-map (0.91+/-0.13 vs 0.98+/-0.10 (P=0.02)) Conclusion(s): We found decreased FA- and increased ADC-values on DTI of sciatic and tibial nerves in CIDP versus controls suggesting that in CIDP demyelination can be detected by MRI.
