T1  - Fractional anisotrophy using magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of peripheral nerves in CIDP: Effect of treatment with subcutaneous immunoglobulin
T3  - 2015 Peripheral Nerve Society Biennial Meeting. Quebec City, QC Canada.
A1  - Markvardsen L.H.
A1  - Vaeggemose M.
A1  - Andersen H.
Y1  - 2015//
N2  - Chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy (CIDP) is diagnosed based on neurophysiological and clinical examination. Previously, studies have shown that MRI of peripheral nerves in several types of polyneuropathy may be helpful. Diffusion Tensor Images (DTI) with calculation of Fractional Anisotropy (FA) values has shown a higher FA-value of the tibial nerve in healthy subjects compared to CIDP patients. MRI of the peripheral nerves in both thighs (sciatic nerve or peroneal/tibial nerve) was performed using the knee coil on a 3 T Siemens Magnetom Skyra MR-scanner. At each thigh one cross section (20 pct. of the distance from upper patella to superior anterior spine of iliaca) was selected for imaging. Seventeen slices were obtained (slice thickness/distance 4:2mm) performing T2-and DTI-weighted MRI sequences with fat saturation. Data from DTI-weighted images served for pixel-by-pixel calculation of FA-values. Circular region-of-interest (ROI) were manually segmented around the nerves at each image slice, carefully avoiding measurement of surrounding tissue with reference to the high-resolution T2-weighted images (0.3x0.3 mm). Average FA-values was calculated from the nerve ROI for each patient with a pixel resolution of 1.36x1.36mm. MRI was performed before and after 3 months of treatment with GammanormR 16.5% in drug-naive CIDP patients, at an arbitrary time point in CIDP patients during maintenance treatment with GammanormR and in healthy controls. We plan inclusion of 15 SCIG-treated CIDP patients, 10 drug-naive CIDP patients and 15 healthy controls. The study is progressing. 1) A 58-year-old female, diagnosed with CIDP. Treated for 3 months with GammanormR 0.33 g/kg/week. MRI of both thighs showed an overall FA-value of 0.41+/-0.02 vs. 0.44+/-0.04 before vs. after initiation of treatment. 2) A 59-year-old male, diagnosed with CIDP and treated with GammanormR 0.36 g/kg/week for several months. MRI of both thighs showed an overall FA-value of 0.40+/-0.01. 3) A 59-year-old male, healthy control. MRI of both thighs showed and overall FA-value of 0.47+/-0.001. These preliminary results indicate that FA-value is lower in patients with CIDP and probably the FA-value will increase following treatment with GammanormR.
