T1  - Change in ADC and fa values of the normal lumbar spinal root as a function of distance from the junction of the dura mater
T3  - EUROSPINE 2014. Lyon France.
A1  - Miyagi R.
A1  - Sakai T.
A1  - Yamabe E.
A1  - Yoshioka H.
Y1  - 2014//
N2  - Introduction: Diffusion weighted imaging (DWI) and diffusion tensor imaging (DTI) are widely used in the evaluation of the central nervous system and recently have been reported as a potential tool for diagnosis of the peripheral nerve or the lumbar nerve entrapment. The purpose of this study was to evaluate consecutive changes in apparent diffusion coefficient (ADC) and fractional anisotropy (FA) values of normal lumbar nerve roots from the junction of the dura mater. Method(s): The lumbar spinal nerves were examined in 6 male healthy volunteers (mean age, 35 years) with no experiences of sciatica, with a 3.0-T MR unit using a five-element phased-array surface coil. DTI was performed with the following imaging parameters: 11,084.6/ 73.7 ms for TR/TE; b-value, 800 s/mm2; MPG, 33 directions; slice thickness, 1.5 mm; and total scan time, 7 min 35 s. Mean FA and ADC values at all consecutive points along the L4, L5 and S1 nerves were quantified on every 1.5 mm slice from the junction of the dura mater with FT method, as follows: direct measurement of FA and ADC placing a region of interest (ROI) in expected axial DTI with fiber tracking (FT method). Result(s): ADC values of all L4, 5, and S1 nerve roots decreased linearly up to 15 mm from the dura junction and was constant distally afterward. ADC values in the proximal portion demonstrated S1>L5>L4 (p<0.05). On the other hand, FAvalues increased linearly up to 15 mm from the dura junction, and was constant distally afterward. FA values in the proximal portion showed L4>L5>S1 (p<0.05). Discussion(s): Our study demonstrated that ADC and FA values of each L4, 5, and S1 are differed, in the proximal part, it changed almost linearly, otherwise the distal part of far than 15 mmwas almost plateau. Although in the proximal part based on a ROI method, we think the influence of spinal fluid is not avoided. In measurement by the short fiber tracking which we used this time compared with measurement by ROI for every slice, it is thought that it is hard to be subject to the influence of spinal fluid, and it seems that it is useful catching a detail change of ADC and FA values by the distance of a nerve root. Conclusion(s): Our study demonstrated that ADC and FA values of each L4, 5, and S1 at the proximal portion from the junction of the dura matter changed linearly.
