T1  - Axonal injury detected using diffusion MRI
T3  - 2011 Meeting of the Peripheral Nerve Society. Potomac, MD United States.
A1  - Song S.-K.
Y1  - 2011//
N2  - Directional diffusivities derived from diffusion tensor imaging (DTI) measurements describe water movement parallel to (lambda, axial diffusivity) and perpendicular to (lambda-, radial diffusivity) axonal tracts. It has been demonstrated that decreased lambda is associated with axonal injury, and increased lambda- is associated with myelin damage. A brief description will be presented on how to apply and interpret diffusion MRI biomarkers of axon and myelin injury.
