T1  - Fragile X-associated tremor/ataxia syndrome-with dominant of neuroimaging findings-the second Polish case
T3  - 21st Meeting of the European Neurological Society. Lisbon Portugal.
A1  - Dolgan A.
A1  - Koszewicz M.
A1  - Budrewicz S.
A1  - Podemski R.
A1  - Chojdak-Lukasiewicz J.
A1  - Hofman A.
A1  - Slotwinski K.
A1  - Szewczyk P.
Y1  - 2011//
N2  - The fragile X-associated tremor/ataxia syndrome (FXTAS) is a newly (in 2001) discovered late-onset neurodegenerative disorder caused by a premutation in the FMR1 X-linked gene. FXTAS is characterized by progressive intention tremor and gait ataxia, with more variable associated features of parkinsonism, dysautonomia, peripheral neuropathy and dementia. In the literature there are a few reports of FXTAS. We report a second case in Poland. Case report: 59-year-old man, with hypertension, has suffered from rest tremor of a right upper limb since 4 months. His grandchild has been diagnosed with fragile X syndrome. On admission to the Neurological Department of Medical University in Wroclaw he presented extra-pyramidal signs: masked face, postural and right upper limb muscles rigidity, rest tremor of a right upper limb; there were no evidence of ataxia, pyramidal signs or sphincter disturbances. Conventional brain MRI showed mild cerebellar atrophy, symmetric high signals in the middle cerebellar peduncles (MPC sign). In perfusion weighted imaging (PWI) hypoperfusion in the middle cerebellar peduncles was revealed, while damage of white matter in MPC and in the internal capsule was seen in diffusion tensor imaging (DTI). Surface electromyography (EMG) revealed rest tremor with frequency of 5 Hz, without other, important electrophysiologic findings. The diagnosis of FXTAS was confirmed by genetic test. Discussion(s): Although our patient showed only small clinical criteria of FXTAS, the diagnosis was based on a big, neuroradiological criteria as well as genetic findings. The authors indicate to themeaning of radiological diagnostics in the FXTAS recognition.
