N2  - The proceedings contain 48 papers. The topics discussed include: endovascular treatment of blood blister-like aneurysms: initial experience with stent-assisted coil embolization; endovascular treatment of cerebral aneurysms with the pipeline embolization device; protective stenting in skull base tumors; rate of recanalization of large intracranial arteries in acute stroke - a comparison of i. a. thrombolysis monotherapy, the penumbra system and solitaire stent; multi-level MR neurography of traumatic plexus injuries: more than imaging of root avulsions; mMR neurography reveals accumulating intraneural microlesions underlying peripheral neuropathy of neurofibromatosis type II; cardiac-gated phase-contrast magnetic resonance imaging in the diagnosis of syringomyelia; individual MRI segmentation reveals enlarged auditory cortex in Williams syndrome as a neural substrate of training-independent musicality; and novel fMRI paradigm for emotion processing in neuropsychiatric disorders.
