T1  - Osteomyelitis in children
A1  - Kaplan S.L.
Y1  - 2005//
N2  - Osteomyelitis is one of the more common invasive bacterial infections in children leading to hospitalization and prolonged antibiotic administration. Over the past decade, increasing microbial virulence, diminishing antibiotic susceptibility, and advances in diagnostic molecular microbiology and imaging techniques have led to changes in the clinical management of children with suspected osteomyelitis, which are reviewed in this article. © 2005 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
